---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import Cta from '../components/Cta.astro';
---
<Base title={"Firm"} description={"About Valley Capital Partners, an investor in hospitality, multifamily, and retail real estate that also buys non-performing loans."}>
<Hero eyebrow={"The firm"} title={"An investor in hospitality, multifamily, and retail."} lead={"Valley Capital Partners buys real estate and the loans secured by it, including loans that have stopped performing or cannot be repaid at maturity. Hospitality, multifamily, and retail are our focus."} />
<main id="main">
<section class="section" id="sectors"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Where we invest</p><h2>Three property types, and the loans behind them.</h2>
    <p>We buy the property or the loan, whichever the situation calls for, and we tell the seller which one we are bidding on.</p></div>
  <div class="cells">
    <div><h3>Hospitality</h3><p>Hotels and the loans secured by them, branded or independent. Our Library, blog, and underwriting page are written about this sector.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Multifamily</h3><p>Apartment properties and the loans secured by them.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Retail</h3><p>Retail properties and the loans secured by them.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section alt" id="capital"><div class="wrap intro">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">Capital</p><h2>Funded by a private family office and committed firm capital.</h2>
    <div class="body"><p>Our acquisitions are funded by a private family office, whose principal has a founding background in online travel and hospitality, and by the firm's own committed capital.</p>
    <p>We identify our capital source to sellers under a confidentiality agreement as part of the bid process.</p></div></div>
  <dl class="pillars">
    <div><dt>No financing contingency</dt><dd>We do not rely on third-party lenders to close a purchase.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Proof of funds</dt><dd>Provided with a bid, or earlier on request under a confidentiality agreement.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Hospitality background</dt><dd>The capital behind the firm comes from a career in the hotel and travel business.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="wrap intro">
  <div><p class="eyebrow">Notes</p><h2>When we buy a loan, we work on the loan, with the property as our measure of value.</h2>
    <div class="body"><p>Buying a troubled loan is different from buying a building or making a new loan. It requires reading a loan file closely, understanding how remedies work in a given state, and knowing what a brand, a manager, and a receiver each need for a hotel to keep operating.</p></div></div>
  <dl class="pillars">
    <div><dt>Sourcing</dt><dd>Direct relationships with banks, receivers, creditors' rights counsel, and special servicers.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Underwriting</dt><dd>Property-level valuation and a legal review of every loan file before purchase.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Asset management</dt><dd>Direct negotiation with owners, supported by counsel in the hotel's state.</dd></div>
  </dl>
</div></section>

<section class="section alt" id="role"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="head"><p class="eyebrow">Our role in a transaction</p><h2>We tell you which seat we are in.</h2>
    <p>We confirm our role in writing before any engagement or agreement.</p></div>
  <div class="cells">
    <div><h3>Principal buyer</h3><p>We purchase the loan or the hotel for our own account and own it after closing.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Capital provider</h3><p>We fund a hotel owner's discounted payoff or recapitalization, secured by the property.</p></div>
    <div><h3>Arranger</h3><p>Where a situation falls outside what we hold ourselves, we introduce another capital source for a fee disclosed in advance.</p></div>
  </div>
</div></section>
</main>
<Cta title={"Speak with a principal of the firm."} text={"We respond to every inquiry directly."} label={"Contact us"} />
</Base>
